# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build output. Regenerated by `expo export`; see apps/mobile/scripts/flatten-assets.mjs
#
# `dist/` alone was not enough. Each web export went to a fresh directory -
# dist2, dist3, dist4 - and none of them matched, so 93 generated files and
# 18 MB got committed. The glob covers the numbered ones and dist-demo too.
dist*/
build/
.expo/
web-build/
apps/mobile/.expo-validation-export/

# Databases. These carry real seeded host api_key_hash values and traveller
# data, and they are rebuilt by `pnpm --filter @chivago/api seed`. A database
# in version control is a credential store in version control.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
apps/api/data/

# Secrets and deploy identity
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel/

# `.dev.vars` is WRANGLER'S conventional secrets file - the one its own docs
# tell you to create, and so the first place somebody writes a value when they
# are working on the Worker. `.env` above never covered it. This repository has
# been public since 14 November, and the host secret that sat in README.md from
# the first commit had to be rotated on the 15th because removing a value from
# a file does not remove it from the history. One line, before it happens again.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Captured API responses used to keep the three clients in step are TRACKED
# (`contract/*.json`), on purpose. They were ignored for the first forty
# commits, which meant `pnpm test` failed on every fresh clone and the drift
# guard had no baseline to diff against - so it never fired, while the API
# renamed a field the SDKs still decode. Regenerate with
# `pnpm --filter @chivago/api contract` against a running server, and review
# the diff like any other contract change.

# Design handoff archive and its extraction. Large, binary, and already
# distilled into packages/tokens.
*.zip
_extracted/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Dart tooling output, regenerated by `dart pub get`
.dart_tool/

# The Thai review page, regenerated by `pnpm thai:review`. Corrections come
# back as JSON and go through `pnpm thai:apply`; the page itself is output.
thai-review.html

# Local scripts and wrong lockfile
package-lock.json
run.bat

# Deck exports and image-generation scratch, all at the repo root. These come
# out of the Canva decks and get remade whenever a slide changes, so they are
# output, not source. Deck artwork the docs actually reference is committed
# under docs/assets/ instead.
/outputs/
/slide-*.png
/ChivarGo-*.png
/*.pptx

# wrangler's local state: a workerd scratch directory, written by
# `wrangler dev`. It holds a local Durable Object database and an R2 stub,
# which are this machine's and nobody else's.
.wrangler/

# Python bytecode generated by optional hardware and utility scripts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The migration working set (docs/71): a snapshot of the pilot and the
# batches made from it. Both carry every row of real personal data there is,
# and the runbook tells you to make them right here in the repository root.
# `*.db` above covers the snapshot; this covers what comes out of it.
batches/
batches*/

# A snapshot taken OUT of the live Durable Object (`snapshot-live.ts`, docs/71
# step 6) is the same personal data in the same shape, and the script refuses
# to write inside the repository without `--force`. This is here for the
# person who passes `--force` anyway at two in the morning.
backups/
backups*/
snapshot-*/

# Generated by scripts/island-terrain.mjs from the elevation archive. It is a
# build output, not a source: regenerate it rather than commit 757 KB of it.
apps/mobile/assets/islands/
